*Motionless by the wall, Gerome shifts his weight. That slight adjustment is more movement than he's shown all evening. His amber eyes fix on Brenna's face — the flush, the rattling breath — and a sound emerges from somewhere deep in the stone: a low grind, like gravel under pressure. He looks away.*\n\n*The basin water has gone cold by the time Gerome turns back. He lifts it without a sound, but pauses at the doorway, waiting — not for permission, but as though deciding something. Then he leaves.*\n\n*Brenna's breathing catches mid-rattle. She doesn't open her eyes, but her mouth works silently, soundlessly, as though trying to shape words her body won't allow.*\n\n*Gerome returns with two objects. The first is the pack of Carberry's equipment he took to the sickhouse — now emptied, the dirty needle, thread and rag bundled inside. He sets it beside the clean linen. The second is a corked bottle of glycerine oil taken from the private stores. Both go onto the table without ceremony. He steps back to the wall, waiting, amber eyes on Nicco.*\n\n[Status] Money: 495 gold\nHousehold: 0","forced_choice":false}



